AT_SETUP([An I/O error without FILE STATUS in a CALLed program stops the run unit])

dnl abort-on-io-exception is enabled by default: an OPEN error of a file that
dnl has no FILE STATUS clause runs the default error handler and STOP RUN.
dnl The STOP RUN must unwind through the calling program, whether the run unit
dnl was started by main() or by a Java caller.
AT_DATA([mainp.cbl], [
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. mainp.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           DISPLAY "before call".
           CALL "subp".
           DISPLAY "after call".
           GOBACK.
])

AT_DATA([subp.cbl], [
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. subp.
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT F ASSIGN TO "no-such-file.txt"
                  ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD F.
       01 R PIC X(10).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           DISPLAY "sub start".
           OPEN INPUT F.
           DISPLAY "sub after open".
           EXIT PROGRAM.
])

AT_CHECK([cp ../../multithread.src/harness/ThreadHarness.java .])
AT_CHECK([javac ThreadHarness.java])
AT_CHECK([${COBJ} mainp.cbl subp.cbl])
AT_CHECK([java mainp], [1], [before call
sub start
], [ignore])
AT_CHECK([java ThreadHarness mainp 3 1 2>/dev/null], [0],
[3 before call
3 sub start
return-code 1 x3
alive
])

AT_CLEANUP
